===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʰedʰ-}}
{{inh+|en|enm|good}}, from {{inh|en|ang|gōd}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*gōd}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*gōdaz}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*gʰedʰ-||to unite, be associated, suit}}.

Cognate with {{cog|ru|го́дный||fit, well-suited, good for; (coll.) good}}, {{m|ru|год||}}, "year", via "suitable time".

Related to {{m|en|gather}} and {{m|en|together}}, but not to {{m|en|god}}/{{m|en|God}}.

Eclipsed non-native {{ncog|enm|bon}}, {{m|enm|bone}}, {{m|enm|boon}}, {{m|enm|boun|t=good}} borrowed from {{ncog|fro|bon|t=good}}, from {{ncog|la|bonus|t=good}}.

