#: {{ux|en|The best is the enemy of the '''good'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|He is an influence for '''good''' on those girls.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Psalms|4|6|passage=There be many that say, Who will show us any '''good'''? Lord lift thou up the light of thy countenance upon us.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1788|author=w:John Jay|journal=w:The Federalist Papers|issue=64
|passage={{...}}the government must be a weak one indeed, if it should forget that the '''good''' of the whole can only be promoted by advancing the '''good''' of each of the parts or members which compose the whole.}}
